      "name": {
        "name": "GPI transamidase component PIG-T",
        "short": "PIG-T"
      },
      "description": [
        {
          "text": "<p>Phosphatidylinositol-glycan biosynthesis class T protein (PIG-T, also known as Gpi16 in budding yeasts) is a component of the glycosylphosphatidylinositol (GPI) trans-amidase complex that adds GPIs to newly synthesized proteins [[cite:PUB00009845]]. Mammalian GPI transamidase consists of at least five components: Gaa1, Gpi8, PIG-S, PIG-T, and PIG-U, all five of which are required for its function. It is possible that Gaa1, Gpi8, PIG-S, and PIG-T form a tightly associated core that is only weakly associated with PIG-U. The exact function of PIG-S is unclear [[cite:PUB00044439]].</p>",
          "llm": false,
          "checked": false,
          "updated": false
        }
      ],
